Kaelen: "Alright. Think. If I'm inside some kind of constructed world, there are rules. Patterns. Weaknesses I can find and use." 2.3. Sequence 2: First Contact — The Glitch-Witch2.3.1. Entity Spawn EventKaelen attempts to exit the crater via the "Golden Path." A trigger volume is breached, causing the first NPC, Elara, to spawn. She does not walk into the frame; she "pops" into existence with a graphical stutter and a particle effect resembling static noise.2.3.2. Character Profile: ElaraElara is the "Glitch-Witch," a deconstruction of the "Magical Girl" trope.Visuals: She wears the flowing robes of a standard RPG sorceress and carries a wooden staff. However, her left arm is partially wireframe, rendering only the geometric mesh without textures.Animation: Her idle animation loops perfectly, but periodically her model "glitches," stretching infinitely into the Z-axis for a single frame before snapping back.Backstory: Originally a standard NPC guide designated by the system, she "broke" her script by saving a previous hero destined to die, fracturing her mana core.2.3.3. Initial Dialogue InteractionThe dialogue system (powered by the custom DialogueManager with typewriter effect and Space-to-advance) initiates. Elara's text is displayed in purple, contrasting with the system's cyan.Elara: "Oh! Another new face? That's unusual. I make a point of remembering faces, and yours... isn't anywhere in my collection."Kaelen: "...Who are you? And how did you just appear out of nowhere. You weren't walking — you just popped in."Elara: "Elara. Glitch-Witch, self-appointed guardian, part-time disaster. I used to have a purpose around here, but I went off-script about... oh, a very long time ago. Now I just wander."Kaelen: "Your arm. It's not... solid. I can see through it. Like the surface didn't finish forming."Elara: (She looks at her glitching arm and smiles beamingly.)
